		<descript>
			<abstract>The Esri shapefile CACB_deposits_prospects is a spatial database that provides spatial and descriptive information for copper deposits and prospects hosted in sedimentary rocks of the Central African Copperbelt, Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) and Zambia.</abstract>
			<purpose>The spatial database was created for use in a geographic information system (GIS) as part of Scientific Investigations Series Report 2010-5090-T, which is part of the USGS assessment of undiscovered copper resources of the world. It provides locations of deposits and prospects, in addition to descriptive information for use in a GIS and for estimating undiscovered mineral resource endowments.</purpose>
			<supplinf>The dataset includes information about host rocks, mineralogy, tectonic setting, grade and tonnage for copper, and grade of cobalt, in addition to references.</supplinf>
		</descript>
