		<lineage>
			<srcinfo>
				<srcscale>1:5,000 to 1:2,000,000</srcscale>
				<typesrc>paper maps and digital data</typesrc>
				<srccontr>Sources provided locational (mixed scales) and descriptive information for deposits and prospects. Full references are provided in the accompanying "GIS references.xlsx" file.</srccontr>
			</srcinfo>
			<procstep>
				<procdesc>
DATA COMPILATION: The data were compiled from a variety of sources: published and unpublished, open access and licensed, public and propriety. Information for sites that could not be verified using publicly available data were excluded from the compilation. Data acquired from digital data files were normalized and imported into a single shapefile. Duplicate records for the same site were condensed into a single entry. Point locations for some sites were manually digitized. Group sites were created to represent multiple sites that have been grouped together for the purposes of resource modeling for deposits within 500 meters of each other. These sites can be identified using the “SiteStatus” field in the attribute table.
DATA ATTRIBUTION: Names for deposits and prospects were based upon the name most frequently used in publicly available sources. Alternate names and spellings are provided in the field "Name_other". Information for tonnage and grade were derived from [Data and Models SIR]. Geologic unit information was used using geologic maps and various reports to update the field Unit; our unit coding scheme is based upon work by Cailteux and others (2007), in which they correlated units from Zambia and the Democratic Republic of the Congo.
</procdesc>
